# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` to package.json
- Updated package-lock.json with new dependency tree

### 2. Modified Files

**src/App.jsx**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the root level of the App component, after the ToastContainer
- The Analytics component is now rendered on all pages (both admin and public routes)

## Implementation Details

According to the official Vercel documentation for React applications:
- The `@vercel/analytics` package provides a simple `<Analytics />` component
- The component should be imported from `@vercel/analytics/react`
- The component can be placed in the main App component to track analytics across all pages

The implementation follows React best practices by:
- Placing the Analytics component at the root level alongside other global components
- Preserving all existing code structure and functionality
- Not interfering with existing providers (CartProvider, AuthProvider)

## Testing

✅ Build completed successfully with `npm run build`
✅ No TypeScript/linting errors introduced
✅ All existing functionality preserved

## Next Steps

To enable analytics data collection:
1. Ensure the project is deployed to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Vercel dashboard
3. Select Analytics in the sidebar
4. Click the Enable button
5. Analytics data will start being collected after the next deployment

